sdl3-mixer-fluidsynth
=====================

This crate is a modified version of FluidSynth: a translation into Rust of
parts of FluidSynth 2.5.7 (the SoundFont synthesizer, Copyright (C) 2003
Peter Hanappe and others; see its AUTHORS), as SDL_mixer 3.3.0 vendors it
(external/fluidsynth at SDL_mixer revision
df66ae893c91b0f6fa5d026a195bb278213d007d, https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_mixer,
which is https://github.com/libsdl-org/fluidsynth at revision
b53de2809bc5e4bffdaec59f447f81ba55ce4fe1), and of the parts of gcem 1.18.0
(the GCE-Math C++ library, Copyright (C) 2016-2024 Keith O'Hara) that
FluidSynth computes its lookup tables with, as FluidSynth vendors it there
(sdlorg_fork/gcem).

It is NOT the original FluidSynth or gcem, nor SDL_mixer's copies of them.

How and when they were changed: on 2026-10-17, the parts of FluidSynth's C
and C++ sources that SDL_mixer's FluidSynth decoder (src/decoder_fluidsynth.c)
reaches, built as SDL_mixer's CMake configures FluidSynth (double-precision
samples, no libsndfile, no threads, no audio or MIDI drivers), were
translated function by function into the Rust source files in src/, which
keep the original copyright notices and comments: the synthesizer, its
voices, channels, generators, modulators and tunings, the rvoice DSP,
mixer, reverb and chorus, the SoundFont 2 loader and sample cache, the
MIDI file player, the settings and the lookup tables (with the gcem
functions they are computed with, in src/gcem.rs). Each file says so in a
line under its copyright notice. The translation works on Rust types
(vectors, indices and reference counts rather than pointers and linked
lists, a mutex for the synth's recursive API lock), and does something
defined where corrupt input makes the C code read or write out of bounds,
convert out of range or loop forever (the places marked "FIXME (upstream)"
in the source). Otherwise it renders bit-for-bit what the C code does,
which its tests check against upstream's C built with the same math
functions (upstream compiles its IIR filter with -ffast-math, whose
results depend on the compiler and the CPU; the translation evaluates the
filter as written). Left out, as SDL_mixer doesn't reach them: the audio
and MIDI drivers, the shell and server, the sequencer, the MIDI router,
LADSPA, reading DLS files, compressed (SF3) samples (which a build without
libsndfile ignores too), the player's system timer, the settings' realtime
callbacks, SoundFont unloading and most of the remaining public API. The
changes are freely available as part of
https://github.com/danielpclark/SDL.

License
-------

FluidSynth is licensed under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public
License, version 2.1 or (at your option) any later version: see COPYING
(FluidSynth's LICENSE, verbatim from SDL_mixer). Its source files say so in
their headers; the few without a header (fluid_lfo.c, fluid_dls.cpp, the
gentables sources and some headers) are covered by that LICENSE as part of
FluidSynth. gcem is licensed under the Apache License, version 2.0: see
LICENSE.gcem (gcem's LICENSE, verbatim from SDL_mixer). So is this crate:
its SPDX license expression is "LGPL-2.1-or-later AND Apache-2.0" (the
translation of gcem, src/gcem.rs, is under the Apache License; everything
else is under the LGPL). The Apache License 2.0 is compatible only with
version 3 of the LGPL (the Free Software Foundation considers it
incompatible with version 2.1), so the combined crate is effectively
distributed under the terms of the LGPL 3.0 or later, which FluidSynth's
"or any later version" allows; the SPDX expression stays the components'.

This is, with sdl3-mixer-timidity, one of the parts of the repository that
aren't under the zlib license. sdl3-mixer uses it to play MIDI through its
`fluidsynth` Cargo feature, which is on by default; build sdl3-mixer with
`default-features = false` to leave it (and MIDI) out.

No SoundFonts are bundled. The test data in testdata/ (a small synthetic
SoundFont, MIDI files, broken copies of both, and the list of test cases)
is generated by tools/gen_fluidsynth_testdata.py in the repository.
